#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# asin

#% text
# `asin(x)` gives the principal inverse sine of `x`, in `[-pi/2, pi/2]` for `-1 <= x <= 1`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact values at 0, `1/2`, `1/sqrt(2)`, `sqrt(3)/2`, 1 and their negatives; other exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# Outside `[-1, 1]` the value is complex, with branch cuts on the real axis beyond `-1` and `1`. Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values. `asin` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
asin(1/2)
#% output
#= (1/6)*pi

#% cell
asin(1)
#% output
#= (1/2)*pi

#% cell
asin(0.3)
#% output
#= 0.3046926540153975

#% cell
asin(-sqrt(2)/2)
#% output
#= (-1/4)*pi

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Outside `[-1, 1]`:

#% cell
asin(2.0)
#% output
#= 1.5707963267948966 - 1.3169578969248166im

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(asin(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= 0.3398369094541219370963925133917641

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(asin(x), x)
#% output
#= (1 - x^2)^(-1/2)

#% text
# `asin(x) + acos(x)` is `pi/2`:

#% cell
asin(0.7) + acos(0.7) - pi/2
#% output
#= 0.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sin`, `acos`, `atan`
